(c) On-site technical support during all scheduled performances and rehearsals;
(d) All necessary cabling, power distribution, and rigging hardware for the sound system.

1.2 The detailed equipment list and deployment schedule are set out in Annex A (Equipment Schedule) and Annex B (Deployment Timeline) attached hereto and forming part of this Contract.

1.3 The Vendor shall provide a qualified sound engineer and sufficient crew to ensure safe and professional operation throughout the event. The Company shall be notified in writing of the names and qualifications of the lead engineer and crew at least fourteen (14) days prior to the commencement of setup.

**2. EQUIPMENT SPECIFICATIONS**

2.1 The Vendor confirms that the main sound system to be supplied under this Contract shall be the **LineArray X8** system, manufactured by the Vendor's principal, as specified in the Equipment Schedule (Annex A). This system configuration is a current and controlled specification for the Vendor as of the date of this Contract.

2.2 The LineArray X8 system shall include, but not be limited to:

(a) Main left and right arrays, each comprising 12 LineArray X8 modules;
(b) Subwoofer array comprising 8 LineArray X8-S subwoofer units;
(c) Front fill speakers (4 units) and stage monitor wedges (6 units);
(d) Digital mixing consoles (FOH and monitor) as per Annex A;
(e) System processors, amplifiers, and all necessary drive electronics.

2.3 The Vendor warrants that all equipment supplied shall be in good working order, properly maintained, and meet the manufacturer's specifications. Any equipment that fails during the Festival shall be replaced or repaired by the Vendor within four (4) hours of notification.

2.4 Substitution of the LineArray X8 system or any of its components with alternative equipment is strictly prohibited without the prior written consent of the Company. The Company's decision on any proposed substitution shall be final.

**3. PAYMENT TERMS**

